message.content:
Here is a simple, complete script using **HTML, CSS, and JavaScript**. This runs directly in your web browser without needing a backend server.

It creates a form where users can type a name and a message, and when they click "Save," the input is displayed immediately on the page below.

### How to use this:
1.  Create a new file on your computer named `index.html`.
2.  Paste the code below into that file.
3.  Double-click `index.html` to open it in your browser.

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
    <title>Simple Input Form</title>
    <style>
        /* Basic styling to make it look nice */
        body {
            font-family: Arial, sans-serif;
            max-width: 600px;
            margin: 40px auto;
            padding: 20px;
            background-color: #f4f4f9;
        }
        .container {
            background: white;
            padding: 20px;
            border-radius: 8px;
            box-shadow: 0 2px 5px rgba(0,0,0,0.1);
        }
        h2 {
            text-align: center;
            color: #333;
        }
        .form-group {
            margin-bottom: 15px;
        }
        label {
            display: block;
            margin-bottom: 5px;
            font-weight: bold;
        }
        input, textarea {
            width: 100%;
            padding: 10px;
            border: 1px solid #ddd;
            border-radius: 4px;
            box-sizing: border-box; /* Ensures padding doesn't widen the element */
        }
        button {
            width: 100%;
            padding: 10px;
            background-color: #28a745;
            color: white;
            border: none;
            border-radius: 4px;
            cursor: pointer;
            font-size: 16px;
        }
        button:hover {
            background-color: #218838;
        }
        #output-area {
            margin-top: 30px;
            border-top: 2px solid #eee;
            padding-top: 20px;
        }
        .saved-item {
            background: #e9ecef;
            padding: 15px;
            margin-bottom: 10px;
            border-radius: 4px;
            border-left: 5px solid #007bff;
        }
        .timestamp {
            font-size: 0.85em;
            color: #666;
            margin-top: 5px;
        }
    </style>
</head>
<body>

<div class="container">
    <h2>Submit Your Input</h2>

    <form id="myForm">
        <div class="form-group">
            <label for="username">Your Name:</label>
            <input type="text" id="username" name="username" placeholder="Enter your name" required>
        </div>

        <div class="form-group">
            <label for="message">Your Message:</label>
            <textarea id="message" name="message" rows="4" placeholder="Type something here..." required></textarea>
        </div>

        <button type="submit">Save Input</button>
    </form>

    <div id="output-area">
        <h3>Saved Inputs:</h3>
        <div id="results"></div>
    </div>
</div>

<script>
    // Select the form and the results container
    const form = document.getElementById('myForm');
    const resultsContainer = document.getElementById('results');

    // Listen for the form submission
    form.addEventListener('submit', function(event) {
        // Prevent the page from refreshing
        event.preventDefault();

        // Get the values from the input fields
        const name = document.getElementById('username').value;
        const message = document.getElementById('message').value;
        const date = new Date().toLocaleString();

        // Create a new HTML element to display the data
        const newItem = document.createElement('div');
        newItem.classList.add('saved-item');

        newItem.innerHTML = `
            <strong>${name}</strong> said: "${message}"
            <div class="timestamp">Saved at: ${date}</div>
        `;

        // Add the new item to the top of the list
        resultsContainer.prepend(newItem);

        // Clear the form fields
        form.reset();
    });
</script>

</body>
</html>
```

### Important Note on Data Persistence
This script saves the data **only in your current browser session**.
*   If you refresh the page, the saved items will disappear.
*   If you open the file in a different browser, the data won't be there.

To make the data persist permanently (so it stays after a refresh or is visible to other people), you would need a **backend server** (using Node.js, Python, PHP, etc.) and a **database**. Let me know if you need help setting that up!
